// apps/admin/wrangler.jsonc — Cloudflare Workers with Static Assets, assets-only.
//
// Hosts ONLY the KwikServe ADMIN web export (`npm run build:admin` → apps/admin/dist). The Worker
// name is deliberately unchanged, so this configuration keeps the existing `quickserve` Worker and
// its existing admin URL; only the artifact it serves changes.
//
// WHY THIS FILE MOVED. It used to live at the repository root and point at `./dist`. That was
// correct only while the admin routes lived inside the consumer app. After the admin application
// was separated into apps/admin, the root `./dist` became the CONSUMER export, so the root config
// silently retargeted the admin URL at the wrong application — and a push to main published the
// consumer bundle over the admin portal. Keeping the config next to the app it deploys makes the
// artifact impossible to confuse, and leaving no config at the repository root means a bare
// `wrangler deploy` there now fails closed instead of shipping whatever `./dist` happens to hold.
// (`./dist` is also reused by `expo export --platform android`, so at the root it may not even be
// a web bundle.)
//
// `directory` is relative to THIS file, so "./dist" resolves to apps/admin/dist. Deploy with the
// explicit `npm run deploy:admin`, never a bare `wrangler deploy`.
//
// Supabase remains the backend; there is deliberately no Worker script (`main`), no assets
// binding, no `run_worker_first`, no other bindings and no secrets here.
//
// Routing model: Expo `web.output: "static"` emits one HTML document per route plus literal
// dynamic-route files (e.g. bookings/[id].html) that no host can map to /bookings/<id>. Cloudflare
// serves generated documents directly and falls back to /index.html (200) for unmatched paths so
// Expo Router's client-side matcher resolves dynamic and unknown routes.
//
// Build-time configuration (EXPO_PUBLIC_*) is inlined by Expo at export time and is supplied as
// Cloudflare BUILD variables, never here. Preview URLs stay off until preview/Production
// environment isolation exists (Workers Builds has a single build-variable set).
{
  "$schema": "../../node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "quickserve",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-09-01",
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./dist",
    "not_found_handling": "single-page-application",
    "html_handling": "drop-trailing-slash"
  },
  "workers_dev": true,
  "preview_urls": false
}
